  "totalCreditsNote": "120 cr per the 2026-27 catalog, at least 100 of them in Arts & Sciences and 80 letter-graded (the app doesn't check those two). Confirm with your advisor.",
  "footnote": "Ten courses minimum. Major courses require a letter grade of C- or better; S/U courses and First-Year Writing Seminars do not count. Transfer credit requires application to the Director of Undergraduate Studies; exceptions require an approved written petition. No prerequisites to declare: meet the Director of Undergraduate Studies, prepare a short statement of interests and goals, and build a program with your advisor. Optional honors requires an honors thesis, normally 8 credits across ANTHR 4983, ANTHR 4991, ANTHR 4984 and ANTHR 4992. Apply in junior spring with a topic and faculty sponsor; normally a 3.3 overall GPA and 3.5 major GPA are required (3.0 overall by petition), with no outstanding major incompletes. Human-subjects research usually needs clearance. ANTHR 4910 independent study requires faculty permission and supervision; graduate courses require instructor permission. Confirm their use toward specific major requirements with your advisor.",
